# Firmware Modules and Robust Coding

## Language (honest status)

- **MCU firmware today is C** (CubeMX + HAL + TinyUSB, `enable_language(C ASM)`).
  Do not silently rewrite files to `.cpp` mid-feature.
- **Intended direction is C++** for application/DSP layers when we deliberately
  migrate (extern "C" at HAL/USB boundaries, no heap, same realtime rules).
  Until that migration is an explicit task: **extend in C**.
- **Cardlink host SDK** (`protocol`) stays **C++17**. Do not mix
  that stack into card firmware CMake.

## Extraction — deliberate, not drive-by

Do **not** peel large modules out of `main.c` / `audio_bridge.c` as a side
effect of an unrelated feature. Extraction is its own small branch/merge:

1. **Helpers first** — move real logic into `static` helpers in the same file
   (`Console_CpuLoad_EnableVoices`, etc.). Keep `Console_Exec()` a flat
   dispatcher (see `embedded-cpp-style.mdc`).
2. **Then a new `.c`/`.h`** — one concern per file (`note_bank`, `cs4304`,
   future `console_cmd.c`). Public header = only what callers need.
3. **Register sources** in the card’s **top-level** `CMakeLists.txt`
   `target_sources` — never in regenerated `cmake/stm32cubemx/CMakeLists.txt`.
4. **Behavior-preserving** — same console replies, same audio path; no
   “while we’re here” feature changes in an extraction PR/merge.
5. **Smoke after every extraction** — build; RS485 `n0` / `gain` / `cpuload on|off`;
   confirm I2S/USB still run. Prefer local merge to `develop` when green.

Growing files is OK short-term if helpers stay small and concerns stay clear.
Prefer extraction when a file owns **two domains** (e.g. console + RS485
framing + LED UI all tangled) or exceeds ~1k lines of hand-written logic.

## Robust coding (always, not only in refactors)

- Bounds-check every console/register input; reply `ok:` / `err:` — never
  silent clamp or ignore.
- Fixed-width types; no `malloc`/`new` in firmware; no `HAL_Delay` in ISR/DMA.
- Hot path: no float, no blocking I/O (see `realtime-audio-performance.mdc`).
- Fail loud on init errors (e.g. DAC fail → `LED_R`); don’t continue half-configured.
- Table-driven extension (`switches[]`, enums) over copying if/else blocks.
- Comment **why** (timing, bus turnaround, scope polarity) — not restating code.
- Feature work and extraction/rules commits stay **separate** (`git-workflow.mdc`).
